From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a webview's guest reports its content size

RenderFrameHostImpl::ContentsPreferredSizeChanged drops the report from
any frame with an outer document, so a guest's main frame -- the primary
main frame of an inner WebContents -- never reached
WebContentsDelegate::UpdatePreferredSize, and WebViewGuest never heard
the size the tray sizes an extension's popup from. Let that one frame
through; a subframe, a fenced frame and a guest page holder's page are
still ignored, as WebContentsImpl::UpdateWindowPreferredSize expects.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium;
`guard-extension-tray.sh` measures it on `crux` with the rest of the
engine job.
---
 content/browser/renderer_host/render_frame_host_impl.cc | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/content/browser/renderer_host/render_frame_host_impl.cc b/content/browser/renderer_host/render_frame_host_impl.cc
index cdba20d0ac..ce40985dee 100644
--- a/content/browser/renderer_host/render_frame_host_impl.cc
+++ b/content/browser/renderer_host/render_frame_host_impl.cc
@@ -7612,8 +7612,11 @@ void RenderFrameHostImpl::ContentsPreferredSizeChanged(
     return;
   }
 
-  // Ignore the request if we are aren't the outermost main frame.
-  if (GetParentOrOuterDocument()) {
+  // Ignore the request if we are aren't the outermost main frame -- unless
+  // this is the primary main frame of an inner WebContents, which is what a
+  // Domicile <webview>'s guest is: its delegate is the guest's own, and an
+  // extension's popup in the tray is sized from this.
+  if (GetParentOrOuterDocument() && (GetParent() || !IsInPrimaryMainFrame())) {
     return;
   }
 
